# SUMMARY: This file lists things git should never save or share.
# They are either secret (API keys), large and re-downloadable (data),
# Seisa's own material (the brief), or junk files made by tools.

# The private Python environment. Anyone can rebuild it with `uv sync`.
.venv/
# Secret keys (Seisa LLM key, Companies House key). Never shared (brief rule).
.env
# Downloaded and generated data. Large, and rebuilt by the build command.
data/
# Seisa's brief documents. The brief says "no Seisa code or data" in the repo (D-011).
brief/
# Text copies of the brief made by scripts/extract_brief.py. Also Seisa material.
docs/brief_text/
# Python's compiled-code cache folders. Made automatically, not useful to share.
__pycache__/
# Cache folder made by the test runner.
.pytest_cache/
# Hidden folder-settings file that macOS creates.
.DS_Store
# The project's own copy of the Neo4j program. Re-downloadable with `make neo4j-install`.
tools/
